  "rationale": "Deploying mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together blocks exfiltration. No single control is enough. (1) With mfa:admin, auth_dc and auth_adfs are blocked, so admin_dc and admin_adfs can never be reached. (2) With mfa:dbadmin, auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup each need admin_dc or admin_adfs, which (1) makes impossible. The attacker can still get stolen_dbadmin via ciserver, but without a foothold on db, fileserver or backup, no exfiltrate technique can fire. Why one control fails: mfa:dbadmin alone leaves the path phish -> pivot -> auth_appserver -> kerberoast -> auth_dc -> escalate_dc -> auth_db. mfa:admin alone leaves the path ciserver -> leak_secrets -> stolen_dbadmin -> auth_db. Segmented alone fails because escalate_workstation lifts segmentation, and patches cannot block the stolen_admin escalation paths."
 },
